<title>FRANCE: GEC Alsthom gets Turkey high voltage contract.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom gets Turkey high voltage contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>GEC Alsthom said on Tuesday that it had won a contract worth 10 million Ecus for high-voltage switchgear and transformers in Turkey.</p>
<p>It said in a statement it would deliver the equipment to Turkish company STFA ELTA, which was in turn supplying a turnkey substation to TEAS, a state-owned electricity generating utility.</p>
<p>GEC Alsthom is a venture between Britain's GEC Plc and French Alcatel Alsthom.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
